{"_id": "llm_agent_and_tool--content_generati--n--71714", "text": "{\n    \"generation_id\": \"gen_987654\",\n    \"user_id\": \"user123\",\n    \"prompt\": \"Write a detailed technical documentation about neural networks.\",\n    \"generated_content\": \"Neural networks are computational models inspired by the structure and function of biological neural networks. They consist of interconnected nodes organized in layers. The input layer receives data, hidden layers perform computations, and the output layer produces the result. Activation functions introduce non-linearity, enabling the network to learn complex patterns. Backpropagation is a key algorithm used for training neural networks by adjusting weights based on error gradients. Different architectures, such as convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and recurrent neural networks (RNNs), are designed for specific tasks. Applications include image recognition, natural language processing, and time series analysis. Further research focuses on improving efficiency, robustness, and interpretability of neural networks.\",\n    \"temperature\": 0.75,\n    \"max_tokens\": 300,\n    \"generation_timestamp\": \"2024-02-28T14:15:00Z\"\n}"}
